cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Equity-Informed Access Improvement Simulator for British Columbia"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, synthetic-data capability demonstrator for equity-informed
  health economic evaluation in R: an equity-stratified cohort state-transition
  model with probabilistic sensitivity analysis, distributional cost-effectiveness
  analysis and a household financial-burden extension, plus demonstration
  interrupted time series, regression discontinuity and discrete event
  simulation modules. All data are synthetic.
authors:
  - family-names: Bwanika
    given-names: Christopher
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chrisbwanika/Equity-Informed-Access-Improvement-Simulator-for-British-Columbia"
keywords:
  - health economics
  - distributional cost-effectiveness analysis
  - cohort state-transition model
  - probabilistic sensitivity analysis
  - reproducible research
  - R
